                  "key": "gen_ai.output.messages",
                  "value": {
                    "stringValue": "[{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"parts\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"content\":\"An **agent trace** is a record of what an AI agent did during a task, step by step. It may include the user’s request, the agent’s actions, tool calls and their results, intermediate outputs, and the final response—often with timestamps and performance details.\\n\\nFor example:\\n\\n1. User asks for the weather.\\n2. Agent calls a weather service with a location.\\n3. Service returns the forecast.\\n4. Agent summarizes it for the user.\\n\\nTraces help developers debug failures, understand tool use, and evaluate an agent’s performance. They record observable steps; they don’t necessarily include the model’s private reasoning.\"}],\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}]"
